ENTRY 1: Concurrency and Thread-Safe State Management

------------------------------------------------------

• Engineering Task:

  Designing a thread-safe mechanism to manage active enrollments and waitlist

  promotions in an in-memory ASP.NET Core service.



• Prompt Used:

  "Implement enrollment, dropping, and FIFO waitlist promotion for one course 

  offering using thread-safe state management in ASP.NET Core."



• AI Proposal Summary:

  The AI suggested wrapping state mutations (modifying the enrolled list and 

  waitlist queue) inside an asynchronous `SemaphoreSlim(1, 1)` lock to prevent

  race conditions during concurrent API requests.



• Decision: ACCEPTED

  I accepted the suggestion as `SemaphoreSlim` is lightweight and well-suited for

  in-memory async operation synchronization in .NET.



• Verification Method:

  I ran the automated xUnit test `ConcurrentEnrollments_PreserveCapacityAndInvariants`

  using `Task.WhenAll` to send parallel requests. All tests passed without capacity

  breaches or race conditions.





ENTRY 2: Waitlist Promotion Policy for Ineligible Learners

----------------------------------------------------------

• Engineering Task:

  Defining and enforcing a consistent waitlist promotion strategy when the top 

  waitlisted learner lacks course prerequisites.



• Prompt Used:

  "Define whether an ineligible learner is skipped or remains waiting, and apply 

  that policy consistently during drop promotions."



• AI Proposal Summary:

  The AI proposed a "Skip-and-Retain" policy: when a seat opens, the system 

  evaluates waitlisted learners sequentially. If the first candidate lacks 

  prerequisites, they are skipped for promotion but remain in their queue position.



• Decision: ACCEPTED

  I accepted this policy because it satisfies strict FIFO ordering while ensuring 

  unqualified learners are not enrolled prematurely.



• Verification Method:

  I created unit tests (`Enroll_FailsWhenPrerequisiteNotMet`) and manually 

  triggered `/api/Course/drop` in Swagger UI using test learner L4 to confirm 

  that ineligible learners stay queued while eligible ones are promoted.





